# Rooiberg Wander — environment variables (Part 11.6)
# Copy to `.env` for local dev, and set the same in your host (Vercel) dashboard for deploy.
# NEVER commit `.env` or real keys. PUBLIC_* are exposed to the browser; everything else is server-only.
# Until the PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL + PUBLIC_PAYSTACK_PUBLIC_KEY pair is set, the Rates page shows a
# "booking coming soon" state instead of the live widget (no errors).

# --- Site -------------------------------------------------------------------
PUBLIC_SITE_URL="https://www.rooibergwander.co.za"   # production origin (no trailing slash)

# --- Supabase (region: eu-west-2 / London — decided) ------------------------
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=""           # https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=""      # anon public key (RLS-limited to the availability view)
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=""     # SERVER ONLY — full access; never expose to the client

# --- Paystack (use TEST keys in dev) ----------------------------------------
PUBLIC_PAYSTACK_PUBLIC_KEY=""    # pk_test_... / pk_live_...
PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY=""           # sk_test_... / sk_live_...  (also verifies webhooks)

# --- Email (Resend — decided) -----------------------------------------------
EMAIL_API_KEY=""                                   # Resend API key
EMAIL_FROM="Rooiberg Wander <no-reply@rooibergwander.co.za>"  # verified sender
BOOKINGS_NOTIFY_TO="hanlie@rooibergwander.co.za"               # operator notify address

# --- Booking config ---------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: deposit vs full is now decided AUTOMATICALLY by lead time (lib/pricing.ts): a trip booked
# 45+ days out pays a 50% deposit + 50% balance; inside 45 days pays 100% up front. BOOKING_DEPOSIT_PERCENT
# is retained for reference/rollback but is NO LONGER read by the pricing engine.
BOOKING_DEPOSIT_PERCENT="100"    # (superseded by the automatic split rule above)
HOLD_MINUTES="30"                # how long a pending booking holds its dates before expiring

# --- Operator dashboard (Part 3) --------------------------------------------
# Each admin account is created manually in the Supabase dashboard (Authentication → Users).
# If ADMIN_EMAILS is set, ONLY those addresses may sign in to /admin (defence-in-depth). Leave
# blank to allow any Supabase Auth user (fine for a single-account install). Sign-in/verification
# reuse PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL + PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY — no extra keys needed.
ADMIN_EMAILS=""                  # comma-separated, e.g. hanlie@rooibergwander.co.za,rudolfpretorius@gmail.com
# ADMIN_EMAIL is still read as a legacy fallback if ADMIN_EMAILS is unset (single address only).

# --- Cron (Vercel Cron → /api/cron/*) ---------------------------------------
# Vercel sends `Authorization: Bearer <CRON_SECRET>` to scheduled routes when this is set in the
# Vercel project env. The pre-trip reminder route rejects any request without it. Use a long random
# value. Schedule lives in vercel.json (0 6 * * * — daily; Hobby plan allows once-daily cron only).
CRON_SECRET=""

# --- AI marketing team (CLAUDE.md Part 18) ----------------------------------
# The team drafts only; nothing below is used to publish anything in milestone 1. Never commit
# real values. In production these live in Vercel (tool server) and GitHub Actions secrets (runs).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=""             # Claude API key for the scheduled runs and marketing:sync (GitHub secret)
MARKETING_TOOLS_TOKEN=""         # long random bearer for /api/marketing/mcp; set the SAME value in Vercel
                                 # and in GitHub secrets (marketing:sync stores it in the agents' vault)
# Channel credentials, documented for the publishing milestone. Not read by any code yet.
X_API_KEY=""
X_API_SECRET=""
X_BEARER_TOKEN=""
X_ACCESS_TOKEN=""
X_ACCESS_TOKEN_SECRET=""
META_ACCESS_TOKEN=""             # Facebook Page / Instagram Graph API token
META_PAGE_ID=""
# Google Search Console, read-only (marketing/search-console.ts). The whole JSON key of a Google Cloud
# service account, added to the Search Console property as a Restricted user. GitHub secret.
GSC_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=""
GSC_SITE_URL="sc-domain:rooibergwander.co.za"   # GitHub variable; a URL-prefix property is "https://www.rooibergwander.co.za/"
# EMAIL_API_KEY and EMAIL_FROM (above) also send the daily "drafts waiting" digest to ADMIN_EMAILS.
# Scheduled runs stay dry until the GitHub repository VARIABLE (not secret) MARKETING_LIVE is "true".
